question_text:
Set #1 = {J, K, L, M, E}
Set #2 = {K, L, M, N, O, P}
There are these two sets of letters, and you are going to pick exactly one letter from each set. What is the probability of picking at least one vowel?

The cost per unit of electricity during a 4 year period is as follows:
Year 1, $2 per unit;
Year 2, $3 per unit;
Year 3, $4 per unit;
Year 4, $5 per unit.
If a factory spent equal dollars on electricity each year, what was the average cost of a unit of electricity during the 4 year period?

Set #1 = {A, B, C, D}
Set #2 = {K, L, M, N, O, P}
There are these two sets of letters, and you are going to pick exactly one letter from each set. What is the probability of picking at least one vowel?

One number will be chosen randomly from each of the sets below . If x represents the chosen member of Set X and y represents the chosen member of Set Y, what is the probability that x/yx/y will be an integer?
X = {9, 10, 11, 12}
Y = {2, 3, 4, 5}

The average age of a committee of 8 members is 40 years. A member aged 55 years
retired and his place was taken by another member aged 39 years . The average age of
present committee is;

M = {-6, -5, -4, -3, -2, -1}
T = {-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2}
If an integer is to be randomly selected from set M above and an integer is to be randomly selected from set T above, what is the probability that the product of the two integers will be negative?
